add('pork-pulled-sliders','Smoky pulled pork rolls with crunchy slaw','Pork',300,[('pork-shoulder',1000),('onion',200),('smoked-paprika',2),('brown-sugar',1),('cider-vinegar',2),('water',200),('bbq-sauce',4),('bread-rolls',4),('cabbage',300),('carrots',150),('mayonnaise',2)],[task('Set up the covered roast','pork-shoulder onion smoked-paprika brown-sugar cider-vinegar water','Heat oven to 140°C fan / 160°C conventional. Put onion in a deep ovenproof casserole. Rub pork with paprika and sugar, place on top and pour vinegar and water around it. Cover tightly with an oven-safe lid. Wash hands after raw pork.','Lid fits tightly and liquid sits around the pork.',['Lidded casserole']),task('Cook until it pulls apart','pork-shoulder','Roast for 4–5 hours. Check liquid after 2 hours and add a little hot water if the base is drying; replace lid promptly. '+SAFE+' It must also pull apart easily with two forks; if still firm, continue covered and recheck every 30 minutes.','Pork is cooked through and shreds without force.'),task('Mix the slaw','cabbage carrots mayonnaise','Keep the shredded cabbage. Grate the prepared carrot cubes carefully or chop them very finely. Mix with mayonnaise in a clean bowl and refrigerate until serving.','Slaw is coated and chilled.'),task('Pull and sauce','pork-shoulder bbq-sauce','Rest pork off the heat for 15 minutes. Lift onto a clean board, discard any string and large fatty pieces, then pull apart with forks. Stir through barbecue sauce and enough hot cooking liquid to keep it juicy.','Pork is shredded and moist.'),serve('bread-rolls','Split rolls, fill with hot pork and serve slaw alongside. Larger joints need extra cooking time; use tenderness as well as the temperature check.')],'Slow roasting makes the pork tender enough to pull into smoky rolls.','https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/pulled-pork',['Wheat','Egg','Mustard (mayonnaise)'])
add('pork-toad-hole','Toad-in-the-hole with onion gravy and peas','Pork',75,[('pork-sausages',8),('plain-flour',140),('eggs',3),('milk',220),('vegetable-oil',2),('onion',200),('gravy-granules',3),('water',450),('frozen-peas',300)],[task('Mix the batter','plain-flour eggs milk','Put flour in a bowl. Beat in eggs, then add milk gradually while whisking until smooth. Leave to stand while the oven heats. Do not taste raw batter.','Batter is smooth and pourable.',['Bowl','Whisk']),task('Start the sausages','pork-sausages vegetable-oil','Heat oven to 200°C fan / 220°C conventional. Put sausages and half the oil in a deep metal roasting tin roughly 25 × 30cm. Roast for 15 minutes, turning halfway.','Sausages are beginning to brown; they are not finished.',['Metal roasting tin','Oven gloves']),task('Add batter and bake','plain-flour eggs milk','Using dry oven gloves, set the hot tin on a heatproof surface. Pour batter around the sausages; hot fat may spit. Return immediately to the oven for 30–35 minutes. Keep the oven door shut until the batter is well risen; opening it early can make the batter collapse. '+SAFE,'Batter is risen and set, not wet underneath; sausages are cooked through.'),task('Make gravy','onion vegetable-oil gravy-granules water','Meanwhile soften onion in the remaining oil in a saucepan over medium-low heat for 15–20 minutes, stirring regularly. Make gravy with the measured granules and water, checking the product dilution and adjusting as directed. Stir into onions and simmer for 3 minutes.','Onions are soft and gravy is hot.'),task('Cook peas','frozen-peas','Cook peas in a separate pan following the packet and drain.','Peas are cooked and hot.'),serve('','Cut the toad-in-the-hole into portions using clean utensils; serve with gravy and peas.')],'Crisp Yorkshire-pudding batter, sausages and onion gravy.','https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/toad-hole-4-easy-steps',['Wheat','Egg','Milk','Check sausages and gravy'])
